.TH SDL_ConvertEventToRenderCoordinates 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ConvertEventToRenderCoordinates \- Convert the coordinates in an event to render coordinates.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ConvertEventToRenderCoordinates(SDL_Renderer *renderer, SDL_Event *event);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This takes into account several states:
.PP

\(bu The window dimensions\[char46]
.PP
\(bu The logical presentation settings
.BR "" ( SDL_SetRenderLogicalPresentation )
.PP
\(bu The scale
.BR "" ( SDL_SetRenderScale )
.PP
\(bu The viewport
.BR "" ( SDL_SetRenderViewport )
.PP
Various event types are converted with this function: mouse, touch, pen, etc\[char46]
.PP
Touch coordinates are converted from normalized coordinates in the window to non-normalized rendering coordinates\[char46]
.PP
Relative mouse coordinates (xrel and yrel event fields) are _also_ converted\[char46] Applications that do not want these fields converted should use
.BR SDL_RenderCoordinatesFromWindow ()
on the specific event fields instead of converting the entire event structure\[char46]
.PP
Once converted, coordinates may be outside the rendering area\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I event
the event to modify\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the event is converted or doesn\(aqt need conversion, or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_RenderCoordinatesFromWindow (3)
